---
import MathLayout from '../../../layouts/MathLayout.astro';
import { getPath } from '../../../utils/path';

const lang = 'en';
const currentPath = '/en/university/number-theory';
const title = 'Number Theory';
---

<MathLayout {title} {lang} {currentPath}>
	<article>
		<h1>{title}</h1>
		<p class="intro">Number theory studies the structure and properties of integers. From the simplest counting to the profound mysteries of prime distribution, it reveals the delicate tension between "finite" and "infinite".</p>

		<h2>First Principle: Integers, Addition, Multiplication</h2>
		<div class="concept-card card">
			<p>Starting from the simplest object (1) and operation (addition), continuously generating and infinitely expanding. This is the First Principle's "one-to-many".</p>
		</div>

		<h2>Modular Arithmetic</h2>
		<div class="concept-card card">
			<p>Infinitely many integers, after dividing by a fixed p, can only leave finitely many possible remainders: 0, 1, 2, ..., p-1. This is forcing infinite into finite from outside.</p>
		</div>

		<h2>Important Theorem</h2>
		<div class="theorem-card card">
			<h3>Fermat's Little Theorem</h3>
			<p>For any a not divisible by p: a^(p-1) ≡ 1 (mod p)</p>
		</div>

		<h2>Learning Path</h2>
		<div class="learning-path">
			<div class="path-step">
				<span class="step-num">1</span>
				<div class="step-content">
					<h3>Divisibility</h3>
					<p>GCD, Euclidean algorithm, Bezout's theorem</p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="path-step">
				<span class="step-num">2</span>
				<div class="step-content">
					<h3>Congruences</h3>
					<p>Modular arithmetic, residue systems, Fermat, Euler</p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="path-step">
				<span class="step-num">3</span>
				<div class="step-content">
					<h3>Primitive Roots</h3>
					<p>Existence conditions, indices, discrete logarithm</p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="path-step">
				<span class="step-num">4</span>
				<div class="step-content">
					<h3>Quadratic Residues</h3>
					<p>Legendre symbol, reciprocity, quadratic fields</p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="path-step">
				<span class="step-num">5</span>
				<div class="step-content">
					<h3>Analytic Number Theory</h3>
					<p>Dirichlet series, ζ function, Prime Number Theorem</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>

		<div class="nav-footer">
			<a href={getPath('/en/university')} class="back-link">← Back to University Math</a>
		</div>
	</article>
</MathLayout>

<style>
	.intro {
		font-size: 1.1rem;
		margin-bottom: 2rem;
	}

	.concept-card {
		margin-bottom: 2rem;
	}

	.concept-card p {
		margin: 0;
	}

	.theorem-card {
		margin-bottom: 2rem;
		background: rgba(139, 92, 246, 0.1);
		border-color: rgba(139, 92, 246, 0.3);
	}

	.theorem-card h3 {
		margin: 0 0 0.5rem 0;
		color: #f1f5f9;
	}

	.theorem-card p {
		margin: 0;
	}

	.learning-path {
		margin-bottom: 2rem;
	}

	.path-step {
		display: flex;
		gap: 1rem;
		padding: 1rem 0;
		border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(99, 102, 241, 0.2);
	}

	.step-num {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: center;
		width: 2rem;
		height: 2rem;
		background: linear-gradient(135deg, #8b5cf6, #ec4899);
		border-radius: 50%;
		font-weight: bold;
	}

	.step-content h3 {
		margin: 0 0 0.25rem 0;
		color: #f1f5f9;
	}

	.step-content p {
		margin: 0;
		font-size: 0.9rem;
	}

	.nav-footer {
		margin-top: 3rem;
		padding-top: 2rem;
		border-top: 1px solid rgba(99, 102, 241, 0.2);
	}

	.back-link {
		color: #8b5cf6;
	}
</style>
